# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages path rules.
#
# _headers sets response headers but cannot block a path. Everything in the
# repository root is served by default on these hosts, which would publish the
# CI scripts, the tooling manifests and any source archive sitting in the repo.
# Apache and IIS get the same protection from .htaccess and web.config.
#
# 404 rather than 403 — there is no reason to confirm these paths exist.
#
# Paths are listed explicitly rather than by extension: the splat in these files
# matches everything after it, so a pattern like /*.md does not behave the way
# an extension glob would. If you add a file that should not be public, add it
# here by name.

# Repository tooling
/.github/*            /404.html   404
/scripts/*            /404.html   404
/docs/*               /404.html   404
/node_modules/*       /404.html   404
/.git/*               /404.html   404

# Tooling manifests and internal notes
/package.json         /404.html   404
/package-lock.json    /404.html   404
/.htmlvalidate.json   /404.html   404
/.pa11yci             /404.html   404
/.gitignore           /404.html   404
/README.md            /404.html   404
/SECURITY.md          /404.html   404
/website-production-checklist.md   /404.html   404

# Source archives — these must never be downloadable.
/hague-dixon-A_original.zip        /404.html   404

# Host configs for the other platforms
/.htaccess            /404.html   404
/web.config           /404.html   404
/_headers             /404.html   404
/_redirects           /404.html   404
